158	  // Where tiles already sit, and how tall they were when they were put there.
159	  // Held across runs, because that is what pinning means: this is the memory
160	  // that stops a late arrival moving an early one. The height is kept with the
161	  // place because a pin is only good for the size it was made at — see
162	  // `pinsThatStillHold`.
